WEBVTT

00:00.560 --> 00:02.180
Me! Me!

00:02.480 --> 00:04.650
I want to do it too!

00:06.940 --> 00:09.100
Thank you, Shirakawa-san.

00:09.460 --> 00:10.900
Hmm. Anyone else?

00:11.360 --> 00:15.110
Yeah! If Runachi is doing it, 
then I will too. You, Nicole?

00:15.110 --> 00:17.550
I have work, so I gotta pass.

00:17.550 --> 00:19.950
Oh, right. Okay...

00:22.800 --> 00:23.520
Huh?

00:23.910 --> 00:26.540
Huh?! Why me?

00:31.570 --> 00:34.380
O-Okay, I'll do it.

00:34.800 --> 00:37.340
We need one more. Is there anyone else?

00:39.560 --> 00:41.350
<i>Okay. I got this.</i>

00:42.210 --> 00:44.940
I-I think Ijichi-kun would be a good choice.

00:49.720 --> 00:51.650
Um, Ijichi-kun?

00:56.760 --> 00:59.370
I-I'll do it.

00:59.660 --> 01:01.900
<i>Thank me later, buddy!</i>

01:14.420 --> 01:21.060
<b>Our Dating Story: 
The Experienced You and The Inexperienced Me</b>

02:33.000 --> 02:39.970
<b>Our Running Story:</b>

02:33.520 --> 02:39.970
<b>The Experienced You and the</b>

02:33.830 --> 02:37.940
Okay, please split up into 
your committees and introduce yourselves.

02:34.020 --> 02:39.970
<b>Inexperienced Me Run Together.</b>

02:37.940 --> 02:42.260
The teacher in charge will contact you 
in a few days with the schedule.

02:43.720 --> 02:48.910
Aww, why did Runachi and Kashima-kun 
have to join the pamphlet committee?

02:48.910 --> 02:52.280
If they'd joined us, all the survival game 
players could have worked together.

02:52.280 --> 02:53.070
Right?

02:53.070 --> 02:53.940
Huh?

02:53.940 --> 02:56.060
We had fun together, didn't we?

02:56.060 --> 02:57.650
Oh, I hope you invite me again!

02:57.650 --> 02:59.620
S-Sure.

03:00.360 --> 03:02.660
Um...

03:06.420 --> 03:11.340
<i>I guess this means 
The Friendship Project is underway.</i>

03:13.270 --> 03:16.960
Since we're in the same class, 
I doubt we need introductions.

03:17.440 --> 03:18.890
Let's do this.

03:19.780 --> 03:20.920
Yeah, let's do this.

03:22.210 --> 03:23.320
...let's.

03:26.890 --> 03:33.600
<b><i>Seirin Festival</i></b>

03:27.260 --> 03:32.590
Should we look at the old pamphlets 
to get a general idea of what to do?

03:32.590 --> 03:33.600
I guess so.

03:33.600 --> 03:38.380
It looks like the theme this year is 
"For the Future," so we'll be thinking ahead.

03:38.380 --> 03:40.670
The future, huh?

03:40.670 --> 03:41.570
Hey, Maria.

03:41.570 --> 03:42.270
Huh?

03:42.270 --> 03:44.500
What kind of stuff are you into now?

03:44.500 --> 03:48.120
Huh? Wh-What kind of what?

03:48.120 --> 03:50.360
I mean, like hobbies and things.

03:50.360 --> 03:51.580
Hobbies?

03:52.230 --> 03:54.040
I like watching videos.

03:54.040 --> 03:59.000
Oh yeah? Hey, did you see Burekou's
brand-new dance video?

03:59.000 --> 04:01.200
It might even be funnier than Yarirofi!

04:01.200 --> 04:04.510
Then there's Na-na and 
Yunayuna and Uirin and stuff.

04:05.800 --> 04:08.040
What... language is that?

04:08.510 --> 04:10.310
Uh...

04:11.460 --> 04:14.730
S-So what kind of videos 
do you watch, Kurose-san?

04:15.890 --> 04:17.940
I like game LPs and stuff.

04:17.940 --> 04:18.900
Huh?

04:19.440 --> 04:21.150
Oh, do you know KEN, then?

04:21.150 --> 04:23.550
The guy who used to be a pro gamer?

04:23.550 --> 04:27.450
I watch him because I like stuff like 
<i>Identity 6 </i>and <i>Werewolf Punishment</i>.

04:27.450 --> 04:28.080
Me too!

04:28.080 --> 04:32.120
Recently he did a <i>Sixty-People-Craft</i> one. 
Have you seen it?

04:32.120 --> 04:35.880
I'm not a big fan of
the audience-participation Kids stuff.

04:35.880 --> 04:37.210
I always feel excluded.

04:37.210 --> 04:40.280
They aren't like that at all! 
KEN is the one talking the whole time,

04:40.280 --> 04:42.920
and once you start to get the different 
Kids' personalities, it gets really fun.

04:42.920 --> 04:45.130
One video I recommend is...

04:48.560 --> 04:51.300
Ryuto, what language is that?

04:57.440 --> 05:00.460
How can I help them get along?

04:57.440 --> 05:02.400
<b><i></i>Math</b>

05:00.460 --> 05:01.930
Yo, Yamada.

05:02.400 --> 05:04.860
Stressed out about that Kurose-san again?

05:08.320 --> 05:10.410
<b><i>Ramen Diner</i></b>

05:08.320 --> 05:10.410
<b><i><b>Gekka-ya</b></i></b>

05:08.320 --> 05:10.410
<b><i>Ikebukuro</i></b>

05:08.320 --> 05:10.410
<b><i>Noodles</i></b>

05:09.400 --> 05:10.410
I see.

05:10.950 --> 05:13.120
That does sound like a mess.

05:13.120 --> 05:15.560
You're pretty popular with girls, aren't you?

05:15.560 --> 05:22.150
I guess. I fooled around a lot in high school, 
but that's why I'm a ronin now.

05:22.840 --> 05:26.280
I had a makeover before high school
and suddenly got all this attention.

05:26.280 --> 05:27.800
Who wouldn't take advantage of that?

05:28.960 --> 05:30.510
Check this out.

05:30.510 --> 05:32.220
Me in 9th grade.

05:30.510 --> 05:34.220
<b>Ping-Pong      Regional</b>

05:32.670 --> 05:36.190
My moment of glory, when I won at 
the regional ping pong club tournament.

05:36.190 --> 05:37.540
I looked like a loser, right?

05:38.290 --> 05:42.940
I was really serious about club activities. 
There was only one girl back then

05:43.460 --> 05:45.150
who said she thought I was cool.

05:46.240 --> 05:48.190
So there was someone?

05:48.190 --> 05:49.870
What happened with her?

05:49.870 --> 05:52.540
We dated for a while after I graduated.

05:52.540 --> 05:56.250
She's the one who told me 
to change my hairstyle,

05:56.250 --> 05:58.680
and that's when I suddenly got popular.

05:58.680 --> 06:00.360
So you cheated on her?

06:00.360 --> 06:03.960
No, I didn't dump her that badly.

06:04.840 --> 06:07.050
But I guess it was still pretty bad.

06:07.050 --> 06:10.100
At least for her.

06:18.060 --> 06:22.630
All right, shall we start our second
pamphlet design meeting?

06:23.100 --> 06:25.820
First, about the general concept...

06:25.820 --> 06:27.490
Oh, about that.

06:28.700 --> 06:31.910
I thought we might as well go all out 
and do it really cute like this!

06:31.910 --> 06:35.390
Since it is a festival, 
do it all sparkly and glamorous

06:35.390 --> 06:37.370
with a pink cover and glitter inside!

06:37.370 --> 06:39.340
I'm not so sure about that.

06:39.710 --> 06:42.430
The culture festival isn't just for girls.

06:42.430 --> 06:46.670
We should use a more subdued design 
that won't embarrass anybody.

06:46.970 --> 06:49.520
Something mature, 
that looks toward the future—

06:49.520 --> 06:54.280
Huh?! But we're still in high school! 
It's okay if it's a little cute.

06:54.280 --> 06:57.030
Like, "Look how bright the future is."

06:57.770 --> 07:00.120
W-Wow, you both put a lot of thought into it.

07:00.120 --> 07:01.760
How about you, Ryuto?

07:01.760 --> 07:03.480
What idea did you have, Kashima-kun?

07:03.480 --> 07:05.310
<i>This is bad.</i>

07:05.310 --> 07:08.170
<i>My idea is a lot closer to Kurose-san's.</i>

07:08.870 --> 07:09.700
<i>But...</i>

07:11.910 --> 07:14.650
Sorry! I don't have a clear idea yet.

07:17.370 --> 07:19.080
<b>Staff Room</b>

07:18.200 --> 07:19.080
Oh.

07:19.080 --> 07:22.920
So their opinions are split?
 That would be a problem.

07:22.920 --> 07:27.520
We have to arrange the printing, 
so we need to decide as soon as possible.

07:27.520 --> 07:28.780
I'm really sorry.

07:28.780 --> 07:33.800
With Sports Day also coming up, 
everybody is probably busy.

07:33.800 --> 07:34.890
That's true.

07:36.930 --> 07:40.510
We have a meeting with 
the publisher right after Sports Day.

07:40.510 --> 07:43.350
You have to decide what to do before then.

07:44.600 --> 07:45.450
Okay.

07:47.160 --> 07:50.710
<i>Ugh. I overpromised.</i>

07:56.900 --> 08:00.330
<i>Any way you look at it, 
their designs are polar opposites.</i>

08:01.870 --> 08:03.330
Oh, crap!

08:07.900 --> 08:08.890
Phew.

08:14.050 --> 08:15.180
Kashima-kun?

08:30.550 --> 08:33.720
Wh-What a coincidence. Are you...?

08:33.720 --> 08:35.340
I'm going home from cram school.

08:35.340 --> 08:36.170
What about you?

08:36.170 --> 08:39.120
I, uh, went shopping.

08:39.120 --> 08:43.820
I-I thought a big bookstore would have 
a better selection of study guides.

08:43.820 --> 08:44.670
Oh.

08:49.560 --> 08:53.350
S-So your home is this way too, Kurose-san?

08:53.350 --> 08:57.550
After my mom's second divorce, 
we decided to move back here.

08:58.400 --> 09:01.010
Oh. That's right.

09:01.910 --> 09:03.910
That's also why I changed schools.

09:04.360 --> 09:08.470
My stepfather paid the tuition 
for my last school.

09:08.960 --> 09:12.860
But after the divorce, 
I wasn't his daughter anymore.

09:12.860 --> 09:14.490
He had no obligation to pay.

09:16.420 --> 09:21.320
I picked this school because even though 
it's private, the tuition is cheap.

09:21.720 --> 09:23.830
S-So that's why.

09:23.830 --> 09:25.790
Wait, Kashima-kun.

09:25.790 --> 09:26.630
Huh?

09:27.120 --> 09:29.290
Doesn't that sound a little strange to you?

09:29.290 --> 09:32.830
If tuition was the only issue, 
I still had other options.

09:32.830 --> 09:37.690
So why do you think I went out of 
my way to go to Runa's school?

09:39.440 --> 09:42.040
To Shirakawa-san...

09:42.500 --> 09:43.930
Well, to harass her?

09:43.930 --> 09:45.310
That's not it.

09:46.050 --> 09:49.520
Yes, I did resent her.

09:49.520 --> 09:54.190
Runa had Dad, and she had a great cook—
our charming grandmother.

09:54.190 --> 09:56.430
She had a stable life.

09:56.430 --> 09:58.480
So why only me?

09:58.480 --> 10:02.240
Why did I end up like this, having to 
change my last name and everything?

10:03.760 --> 10:06.960
But the actual reason 
I decided to transfer to this school

10:07.590 --> 10:10.920
is probably because 
I wanted to make Runa happy.

10:10.920 --> 10:12.130
Huh?

10:12.130 --> 10:16.140
Runa likes surprises. As her boyfriend, 
you should know that.

10:16.140 --> 10:17.820
Oh. Yeah.

10:18.340 --> 10:23.160
I said a lot of horrible things to Runa. 
I told her I hated her so many times,

10:23.160 --> 10:25.680
but I think some part of me 
still depended on her.

10:26.470 --> 10:28.140
I believed that Runa would forgive me.

10:28.530 --> 10:32.070
I believed that she'd always be my friend.

10:33.640 --> 10:35.690
<i>That's exactly how I felt that time.</i>

10:35.690 --> 10:40.320
<i>I took advantage of Shirakawa-san's kindness 
and selfishly expected her to forgive me.</i>

10:41.060 --> 10:46.680
I was sure that when Runa saw me walk into 
the classroom, she'd be surprised and happy.

10:46.680 --> 10:50.820
I thought she'd say, "This is my sister!" 
and introduce me to everyone.

10:52.000 --> 10:57.580
So it was a shock. When Runa saw me,
 she only looked confused.

10:57.580 --> 10:59.470
And that's why you did what you did?

11:01.760 --> 11:07.080
I know it was all stupid. 
Everything I did to you and Runa. All of it.

11:07.720 --> 11:11.660
But thanks to that, 
I've stopped trying to fake it.

11:12.200 --> 11:15.670
Like when I was in my old school 
and just acted like myself.

11:16.450 --> 11:20.780
I think I'm starting to get back 
to my normal self again.

11:22.040 --> 11:23.270
That's good.

11:24.800 --> 11:30.460
<i>Just now, I think the discomfort I felt 
around Kurose-san finally disappeared.</i>

11:31.010 --> 11:34.390
<i>Kurose-san cares a lot 
about Shirakawa-san too.</i>

11:35.010 --> 11:36.420
<i>Maybe the two of them really can...</i>

11:36.980 --> 11:39.100
Aren't you coming, Kashima-kun?

11:39.100 --> 11:42.120
Huh? Oh! Yeah, I'm coming!

11:47.030 --> 11:49.100
Do you always go home around this time?

11:49.100 --> 11:53.060
Well, yeah. I always study alone after class.

11:53.060 --> 11:56.020
It's pretty late. Want me to walk you home?

11:56.020 --> 11:58.430
No, it's fine. 
It's not like you're my boyfriend.

11:56.020 --> 11:58.590
Beware of
 Molesters

11:58.430 --> 11:59.480
Whoa!

12:00.420 --> 12:03.200
Sorry, I almost bumped into someone.

12:06.240 --> 12:07.370
Huh?

12:07.940 --> 12:10.330
You go to K. Prep School?

12:10.330 --> 12:12.710
Uh, mm-hmm.

12:10.330 --> 12:13.290
Be Careful 
Not to
 Drop Things

12:14.360 --> 12:16.250
Yeah, I knew.

12:16.250 --> 12:17.180
Huh?

12:17.660 --> 12:19.560
Well, see you at school.

12:20.100 --> 12:20.960
Huh?

12:22.520 --> 12:23.430
Huh?

12:23.430 --> 12:26.390
Huh?!

12:26.680 --> 12:31.380
Geez. You don't need to sneak around 
like that. I'll keep my distance.

12:33.840 --> 12:35.060
Dummy.

12:39.480 --> 12:46.990
m 0 0 l 240 0 240 100 0 100

12:39.480 --> 12:46.990
Runa: 
We always had really
 different interests

12:42.240 --> 12:46.990
Runa:
 Like completely
 opposite

12:42.240 --> 12:46.990
m 0 0 l 135 0 135 80 0 80

12:43.990 --> 12:46.990
m 0 0 l 220 0 220 120 0 120

12:43.990 --> 12:46.990
Runa: 
One time I gave
 her earrings and she
 was like "meh"

12:47.620 --> 12:49.450
It isn't like that at all.

12:49.930 --> 12:55.040
<i>Kurose-san wants to be 
your friend too, Shirakawa-san.</i>

12:55.040 --> 12:57.920
<i>She just has trouble opening up about it.</i>

12:57.920 --> 13:06.890
m 0 0 l 240 0 240 100 0 100

12:57.920 --> 13:06.890
Ryuto: 
It's okay, I'm sure it'll 
go better next time

13:00.630 --> 13:06.890
m 0 0 l 260 0 260 100 0 100

13:00.630 --> 13:06.890
Ryuto:
 I told you I'd help 
with The Friendship Project

13:04.630 --> 13:06.890
Runa: 
Thanks you're
 the best

13:04.630 --> 13:06.890
m 0 0 l 175 0 175 80 0 80

13:10.680 --> 13:15.060
<b>Seirin Private High School
Sports Day</b>

13:15.370 --> 13:16.250
Yoo-hoo!

13:16.250 --> 13:17.100
Go for it!

13:17.100 --> 13:18.620
Fight!

13:19.480 --> 13:22.120
On your marks, get set...

13:23.860 --> 13:25.180
Do it, Runachi!

13:25.180 --> 13:26.570
Go girl! Let 'er rip!

13:34.710 --> 13:39.680
<i>Sports Day. A festival by the popular types,
 for the popular types.</i>

13:39.680 --> 13:42.570
<i>Up to now, I only participated 
because I had to.</i>

13:43.520 --> 13:44.880
<i>But this year...</i>

13:44.880 --> 13:47.590
G-Go for it, Shirakawa-san!

14:03.560 --> 14:04.940
Say "ahh."

14:04.940 --> 14:06.600
Ahh.

14:06.900 --> 14:09.660
<b>Menacing</b>

14:09.660 --> 14:12.620
<i>Today's the day! 
The Seirin High School Sports Day!</i>

14:13.040 --> 14:16.320
<i>Here comes our famous afternoon 
event, the scavenger race!</i>

14:16.320 --> 14:19.470
<i>And this race isn't just about speed! 
Who will find luck on their side</i>

14:19.470 --> 14:22.710
<i>and cross the finish line first? 
Who'll take the win?</i>

14:23.250 --> 14:24.420
All right!

14:25.000 --> 14:27.820
Ryuto, come here!

14:27.820 --> 14:28.380
Huh?

14:28.670 --> 14:30.410
Um, me?

14:30.410 --> 14:31.850
Hurry up and get going.

14:31.850 --> 14:34.040
But a scavenger item...?

14:35.520 --> 14:37.050
Full speed ahead!

14:37.050 --> 14:38.440
Uh, yeah!

14:40.440 --> 14:41.820
<i>I like Runa.</i>

14:42.320 --> 14:44.940
<i>She races like a sports car.</i>

14:45.330 --> 14:48.840
<i>I want to go everywhere with her!</i>

14:56.800 --> 14:58.430
We did it, Ryuto!

14:58.430 --> 15:00.380
We did! Congrats!

15:00.380 --> 15:04.880
Shirakawa-san, today you w-were really great!

15:04.880 --> 15:07.080
We won together, you know.

15:07.080 --> 15:11.590
Even when I was running the foot 
race alone, you cheered me on.

15:11.590 --> 15:14.650
Huh? You heard me?

15:16.100 --> 15:18.810
I'm glad I got to run with you, Ryuto!

15:18.810 --> 15:21.520
<b>Somebody
 You 
Like</b>

15:23.730 --> 15:25.130
Runa!

15:25.130 --> 15:26.690
Get over here!

15:28.900 --> 15:30.610
<b><i>Girls' Dressing Room</i></b>

15:31.820 --> 15:34.530
Wow! You look awesome!

15:34.530 --> 15:37.000
And those slender arms! And long legs!

15:37.000 --> 15:40.500
Oh, come on. You look great too!

15:40.500 --> 15:43.740
Thank you! But I am a little surprised.

15:43.740 --> 15:46.810
I never imagined you as the cheerleader type.

15:46.810 --> 15:51.220
I'm sorry. When you did sign-ups in class,
 I couldn't work up the courage.

15:51.220 --> 15:53.800
It's fine, it's fine! 
I'm just glad you're here!

15:54.220 --> 15:55.930
Now let's blow their minds!

15:59.250 --> 15:59.980
Yeah!

16:01.280 --> 16:04.560
Oh yeah? So your mom came to watch?

16:04.560 --> 16:08.080
Yeah. This year, she said 
she'd take time off work to come.

16:08.080 --> 16:11.280
Is that maybe why you 
volunteered for the cheer team?

16:13.060 --> 16:15.080
No way. Seriously?

16:15.080 --> 16:17.230
Sorry. I know it sounds cringe.

16:17.230 --> 16:20.760
A high schooler asking her mom to come watch.

16:20.760 --> 16:22.500
Nah, that isn't cringe!

16:22.500 --> 16:24.410
I love my mom too.

16:24.410 --> 16:28.060
And it's such a cute uniform. 
Of course you'd want her to see!

16:30.130 --> 16:31.420
What's wrong now?

16:37.040 --> 16:38.080
Do you...

16:38.080 --> 16:40.350
Sorry, I think I forgot something.

16:40.350 --> 16:41.350
Huh?

16:41.720 --> 16:45.060
I'll be back in time for the cheer battle!

16:46.180 --> 16:47.770
Kurose-san...

16:47.770 --> 16:51.880
Listen, Mom! I get to run 
in the last relay too!

16:51.880 --> 16:56.630
Really? That's great! 
You've always been athletic, Runa.

16:57.580 --> 16:59.450
Say, Runa, where's Maria?

16:59.450 --> 17:00.140
Huh?

17:00.660 --> 17:03.710
Isn't she in your class? Have you seen her?

17:03.710 --> 17:07.150
She said she's cheerleading 
this year and wanted me to come.

17:07.150 --> 17:10.970
You should've seen how hard 
she was practicing at home!

17:10.970 --> 17:14.340
I had to take a half-day at work to make it.

17:16.200 --> 17:18.180
I'll go look for her!

17:18.180 --> 17:19.720
Oh, Runa?

17:19.720 --> 17:21.450
Uh, I'll go with her.

17:24.960 --> 17:26.440
We should split up.

17:26.440 --> 17:27.370
Yeah.

17:42.640 --> 17:45.880
Kurose-san, your mom is here to see you.

17:46.560 --> 17:47.670
I know.

17:48.310 --> 17:52.020
Are you cheerleading? I didn't know.

17:55.000 --> 17:57.050
She's supposed to be <i>my</i> mom.

17:57.550 --> 17:58.230
Huh?

17:58.800 --> 18:03.530
I gave her the handout and asked her to come.

18:03.530 --> 18:07.020
She was supposed to be here to root for <i>me</i>.

18:16.440 --> 18:20.800
How was I supposed to 
react after seeing that?

18:20.800 --> 18:25.080
Nobody in class even knows 
that Runa and I are sisters.

18:26.500 --> 18:28.390
What are you here for?

18:28.390 --> 18:34.550
Your mom is looking for you. She says 
she skipped work to come and root for you.

18:34.980 --> 18:40.040
Mom thinks that Runa 
and I get along at school.

18:40.640 --> 18:45.840
I did something stupid and cruel, 
so I can't tell anyone we're sisters.

18:45.840 --> 18:47.020
I don't want Mom to know that.

18:47.020 --> 18:48.060
I know, but—

18:48.060 --> 18:49.510
Just go!

18:49.980 --> 18:52.190
I know you don't care about me at all!

18:52.190 --> 18:53.900
But I do care!

18:58.360 --> 19:01.030
Because I'm Runa's sister?

19:01.030 --> 19:03.990
That's part of it. 
And because we're teammates.

19:04.450 --> 19:06.490
Just in the pamphlet committee?

19:06.490 --> 19:08.710
And because we're classmates.

19:13.720 --> 19:15.130
I like you.

19:15.470 --> 19:16.590
Huh?

19:16.590 --> 19:18.920
I still like you, Kashima-kun!

19:18.920 --> 19:22.140
So please don't make me like you more!

19:22.520 --> 19:25.760
You don't want that, right? So just go.

19:25.760 --> 19:27.880
Stop being so nice to me!

19:34.280 --> 19:37.180
I know how you feel, Kashima-kun.

19:37.760 --> 19:40.610
I don't intend to be 
rejected like that again.

19:40.610 --> 19:43.580
This is only about my own private feelings.

19:43.580 --> 19:46.830
Whoever I want to like, whoever I do like...

19:46.830 --> 19:49.850
I'm free to feel however I want, right?

19:52.290 --> 19:57.750
I just want to like you. 
There doesn't have to be any more to it.

20:08.690 --> 20:13.960
For the cover, I took both of your 
suggestions and made two samples.

20:12.890 --> 20:17.900
<b>Seirin Festival</b>

20:13.960 --> 20:17.900
Wow, this is so cute! No wonder 
you're a professional designer.

20:17.900 --> 20:20.760
You're just saying that 
because it's the one you like.

20:20.760 --> 20:23.860
This one has broader appeal. 
And better style.

20:23.860 --> 20:27.930
They're both lovely, but it's time 
you made up your minds.

20:27.930 --> 20:29.580
We have to decide today.

20:29.580 --> 20:35.290
Hmm. If I were a high school student, 
I'd think this one was more exciting.

20:35.290 --> 20:40.410
But for the boys and parents, 
this is clearly the better choice.

20:40.960 --> 20:42.490
What do you think, Kashima-kun?

20:42.490 --> 20:44.510
You're the spokesperson here 
for male students, after all.

20:44.510 --> 20:46.800
Well, let's see.

20:47.220 --> 20:49.960
<i>To tell the truth, I'm on Kurose-san's side.</i>

20:49.960 --> 20:51.350
<i>However...!</i>

20:54.410 --> 21:01.370
Since the theme of this year's, um, 
culture festival is "For the Future,"

21:02.280 --> 21:07.880
in the spirit of a "rosy" future, maybe 
a flashier design would have, I don't know,

21:07.880 --> 21:09.740
a different kind of impact.

21:09.740 --> 21:11.080
That's enough, Ryuto.

21:11.080 --> 21:12.130
Huh?

21:12.130 --> 21:13.450
Tell us what you really think.

21:13.860 --> 21:16.920
I don't want you to lie for me.

21:19.520 --> 21:23.590
Kashima-kun, it's best 
if you state your honest opinion.

21:28.240 --> 21:30.230
I think...

21:33.350 --> 21:37.480
if I actually had to carry one around, 
I'd prefer the monochrome version.

23:26.050 --> 23:27.630
On the next <i>Our Dating Story</i>,

23:27.630 --> 23:30.600
the experienced you and the inexperienced me

23:30.600 --> 23:32.220
go different ways.

23:34.160 --> 23:37.560
Love is bleak, y'all. Literal nothingness.

23:37.930 --> 23:39.930
<b>Our Different Story: The Experienced You and the Inexperienced Me Go Different Ways.</b>
